<h2>Inputs and Dropdowns</h2>
<hr>
<p>These elements are commonly used for forms and menus that allow users to fine-tune the data being displayed.
  Elements that are NOT listed here, such as radio groups have not been used in pk-gov yet, and as such may not
  be styled properly compared to other options.
</p>
<h3>STANDARDISE/GLOBALISE INPUT CLASSES FIRST BEFORE DOING THIS PART!</h3>

<h2>PIBSS card</h2>
<hr>
<div class='pibss-card' style='flex: calc(50% - .5rem); gap: 1rem; min-width: 540px; max-width: calc(50% - .5rem); margin-right: auto; display: flex; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-s)'>
  <img src="/assets/pictures/ministers/pbb.webp" alt="pink bear bear" class='pibss-picture' style='aspect-ratio: 3/4; flex-shrink: 0; flex-basis: 180px; min-width: 0; height: auto;'>
  <div class='pibss-card-text' style='flex-direction: column; width: 100%; min-width: 0; display: flex;'>
    <h2 class='pibss-name' style='line-height: var(--line-height-condensed); font-size: var(--font-size-xl); display: inline-block; position: relative; overflow: clip;'>Pink Bear Bear</h2>
    <p class='pibss-type' style='font-size: var(--font-size-s); display: inline-block; position: relative; overflow: clip; margin-bottom: 0'>Type: Bear Bear</p>
    <p class='pibss-country' style='font-size: var(--font-size-s); display: inline-block; position: relative; overflow: clip; margin-bottom: 0'>Origin Country: Malaysia</p>
    <p class='pibss-date' style='font-size: var(--font-size-s); display: inline-block; position: relative; overflow: clip; margin-bottom: 0'>Date Joined: 22 Oct 2008</p>
    <p class='pibss-location' style='font-size: var(--font-size-s); display: inline-block; position: relative; overflow: clip; margin-bottom: 0'>Residence: Big Tent Plains</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>Not to be confused with 'regular' cards, these elements are used to display a plushie's data in PIBSS, and
  should NOT be used for any other purpose. A PIBSS card is usually created dynamically with JavaScript as
  data has to be fetched from the PIBSS database, resulting in a structure similar to the example shown below
  (note that PIBSS cards are automatically animated when the relevant classes are added, except for the example
  above):
</p>
<pre>
  &lt;div class='pibss-card'&gt;
    &lt;img src="image/here" alt="who's there?" class='pibss-picture'&gt;
    &lt;div class='pibss-card-text'&gt;
      &lt;h2 class='pibss-name'&gt;Plushie name&lt;/h2&gt;
      &lt;p class='pibss-type'&gt;Type: ?&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;p class='pibss-country'&gt;Origin Country: ?&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;p class='pibss-date'&gt;Date Joined: ?&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;p class='pibss-location'&gt;Residence: ?&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
</pre>

<h2>Side-by-side text and image</h2>
<hr>
<p>Sometimes, having an image besides text can improve the content, rather than having the image before or
  after the text block. Examples can be found in the 'Who we are' and 'Safety and Residency' pages, where
  text and an image appear side by side on larger viewports, but appear in sequence on smaller viewports. 
  This can be done by using the <code>'.side-by-side'</code> class as shown below:
</p>
<pre>
  &lt;div class='side-by-side'&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Text content goes here&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;img src="image/here" alt="who's there?"&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
</pre>